    "diversity": "There is support for students who demonstrate a sincere interest in working in under-served medical communities or reducing health disparities in under-represented populations and students from non-traditional backgrounds. \n\nhttps://www.unmc.edu/student-success/student-life/slido.html\nhttps://www.unmc.edu/oce/engagement/index.html",
    "leaveOfAbsence": "Students may, under exceptional circumstances, be granted a Leave of Absence. Any LOA granted shall be solely within the discretion of UNMC based upon the merits of the request.",
    "organizationActivities": "There are many student organizations on campus in which students can get involved. For a complete list: https://unmc.campuslabs.com/engage/organizations",
    "setting": "UNMC College of Medicine Omaha - is located in the heart of Omaha, in the thriving Blackstone District. This lively and growing restaurant and entertainment district is steps away from our campus. Other recreational and cultural activities include the Omaha Symphony Orchestra, the Old Market, the Joslyn Art Museum, the Omaha Community Playhouse, the Opera Omaha, and the Henry Doorly Zoo. Omaha is the home of the College Baseball World Series.\n\nUNMC College of Medicine Kearney -  is an ideal fit for students interested in rural primary care, but also for students wanting to pursue a specialty field of medicine while living and working in Greater Nebraska, providing much-needed health care to Nebraska\u2019s rural citizens. The medical curriculum is identical to that of the Omaha campus \u2013 the same course structure, assessments/evaluations, graduation requirements and policies. There only is one UNMC College of Medicine and one medical school curriculum, which now is offered on two campuses. ",
    "housing": "Campus housing and apartments are available and within walking distance.",
